;; ebb's conformance registry -- the machine-readable half of doc/conformance.md.
;;
;; doc/conformance.md is the prose. This file is what test/ebb/conformance-test
;; can check, so the prose cannot rot away from the code (ebb-8nq.22). It follows
;; jolt's own test/conformance/known-divergences.edn pattern: a divergence that
;; is not listed is a bug, not a feature, and adding one is part of the change
;; that causes it.
;;
;; WHAT THE GATE CHECKS, and what it cannot.
;;
;; It cannot detect an unlisted divergence -- that would need missionary as an
;; oracle, and missionary needs a JVM, which is the whole thing ebb does without.
;; (There IS an oracle available to a developer: see the recipe in ebb-8nq.38's
;; notes. It is not something CI can depend on.) What the gate does enforce is
;; that the registry cannot ROT:
;;
;;   * every :pinned-by names a test var that still exists, so a divergence
;;     whose test is deleted or renamed fails the suite rather than going quiet;
;;   * every :id appears in doc/conformance.md, so an entry whose prose is
;;     deleted fails;
;;   * every id marked in doc/conformance.md appears here, so prose cannot
;;     describe a divergence the registry has never heard of;
;;   * an entry with no test has to say WHY in :unpinned, which is the useful
;;     discipline -- most of those turn out to be statements about the host or
;;     about cost rather than about behaviour a test could catch.
;;
;; :kind is :api, :behaviour, :host, or :harness.

[{:id       :cancelled-is-a-value
  :kind     :api
  :summary  "missionary throws missionary.Cancelled; jolt has no user classes, so ebb throws an ex-info carrying ::ebb.impl.util/cancelled. Use m/cancelled?."
  :pinned-by ebb.sp-cancel-test/body-can-catch-cancellation-and-succeed}

 {:id       :reactive-streams-is-a-protocol
  :kind     :api
  :summary  "missionary's publisher returns an org.reactivestreams.Publisher; jolt has no Java interfaces, so ebb states the same three roles as protocols in ebb.rs with the same names and contract."
  :pinned-by ebb.pub-test/request-before-ready}

 {:id       :park-at-any-depth
  :kind     :behaviour
  :summary  "cloroutine rewrites ? at the syntactic breakpoint, so missionary cannot park from a function a coroutine calls (#127, undefined upstream). An ebb sp owns a fiber and ? parks it, so depth is irrelevant. A superset."
  :pinned-by ebb.missionary-issues-test/indirect-breakpoint-calls-are-legal-127}

 {:id       :watch-derefs-on-transfer
  :kind     :behaviour
  :summary  "missionary #89: m/watch takes the new state from the watch callback and can discard the latest value. ebb takes the maintainer's stated fix and derefs the reference on transfer, so it reports whatever the reference holds when the consumer gets there rather than the states the callbacks carried."
  :pinned-by ebb.missionary-issues-test/watch-does-not-discard-the-latest-value-89}

 {:id       :fork-in-finally-refused
  :kind     :behaviour
  :summary  "jolt compiles finally to a dynamic-wind after-thunk, which runs once per re-entry, so a fork captured inside one would run the handler N+1 times for N branches. ebb refuses it with ::ebb.impl.prompt/fork-in-finally rather than running it wrong."
  :pinned-by ebb.prompt-test/forking-inside-a-finally-is-refused}

 {:id       :continuations-are-executor-affine
  :kind     :behaviour
  :summary  "a continuation may only be resumed on the executor that captured it. ADR-001 discipline 2 makes that structural rather than a latent hang."
  :pinned-by ebb.prompt-test/resuming-on-another-fiber-throws}

 {:id       :subscribe-publisher-round-trip
  :kind     :behaviour
  :summary  "(subscribe (publisher f)) is not supported, in ebb or in missionary: Pub calls on-next synchronously from inside request and Sub calls request from inside transfer, so wiring one into the other re-enters the notifier before the pending transfer returned."
  :unpinned "Shared with missionary and not an ebb divergence at all; listed because a reader comparing the two will wonder. Nothing to pin -- the behaviour is that you must not do it."}

 {:id       :ap-cp-cost-a-hop
  :kind     :behaviour
  :summary  "ap and cp pay a scheduling hop per resumption: a callback cannot resume the process inline, it enqueues and the owner fiber picks it up (ADR-001 discipline 2)."
  :unpinned "A statement about cost, not behaviour. ebb-8nq.40 carries the measurements; a test would be a benchmark, and benchmarks do not belong in the conformance gate."}

 {:id       :deftype-field-shadowing
  :kind     :host
  :summary  "a local may not share a name with a mutable deftype field: in some shapes the local reads the FIELD. ebb's convention is to prefix such locals v-."
  :unpinned "A jolt compiler defect (ebb-8nq.24), not an ebb behaviour. Not yet minimised, so there is nothing stable to assert against."}

 {:id       :strings-are-codepoint-indexed
  :kind     :host
  :summary  "(count \"\\ud83d\\ude00\") is 1, where JVM Clojure counts UTF-16 code units."
  :unpinned "A jolt property, inherited wholesale. Asserting it here would be testing jolt, not ebb."}

 {:id       :cas-compares-by-value
  :kind     :host
  :summary  "compare-and-set! on an atom compares by value where JVM Clojure uses identity."
  :unpinned "A jolt property, inherited wholesale. ebb's impls are written not to depend on either reading."}

 {:id       :tck-timeout-is-lowest-priority
  :kind     :harness
  :summary  "missionary's tck check! treats an event raised on the driving thread as reentrant; an ebb ap or cp answers from its owner fiber, so thread identity no longer reflects real-time ordering. ebb's check! delivers a timeout only when no real event is pending."
  :unpinned "The harness cannot test itself. It is exercised by every tck case in ebb.core-test, and getting it wrong showed up there as flakes."}

 {:id       :lolcat-waits-for-declared-events
  :kind     :harness
  :summary  "lolcat's call required every event it declared to be raised before the call returned, which is only true when callbacks run inline on the caller. ebb's callbacks are cast onto an owner fiber, so a call now waits on a promise for up to *event-timeout*. Same events, same order, one instruction later."
  :unpinned "The harness cannot test itself. Every lolcat-driven namespace exercises it; before the change nine of missionary's own ap and cp cases failed."}]
